  "description": "This cocktail is a masterful combination of just three ingredients: spicy whiskey, luscious vermouth, and complex Barolo Chinato, a bittersweet, herb- and spice-dosed digestivo made from one of Italy's best wines. Chocolaty, smooth, and deep, it's subtler than a Boulevardier, though it's in the same family.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: rye whiskey → Japanese whisky\n\nNotes: Derrick initially made this drink with Japanese whisky, but rye is a more affordable (and totally delicious) option. He serves the drink in a glass rimmed with dehydrated orange peel and Campari, but you don't need to get that fancy at home.",
  "author": [
    "Maggie Hoffman"
